-## Keep three document moments separate
+## Who this is for
 
-Exam booking, test day, and a family reunion visa file are different stages. A document that helps you register is not automatically sufficient for the examination, and a course completion record is not the same as an official language certificate.
+Use this checklist after you know the relevant route and have selected an exact exam product or centre to investigate. It separates three document moments that are often wrongly merged: registration, test-day check-in, and the family-reunion visa file. It does not tell you which passport, copy, translation, original, certificate, or additional document your case will require. Those instructions belong to the selected centre and the competent German mission.
 
-The selected local test centre controls its current booking and test-day document instructions. The responsible German mission controls the current visa-file checklist, including any original, copy, translation, or additional-document instruction. This page is a planning aid, not a legal opinion or a decision on what your case requires.
+## Key decisions
 
-## Before booking
+### Keep three owners visible
 
-Confirm your legal name exactly as shown on the identity document you will use, the accepted passport or ID type, a working email and phone number, payment method, and the booking confirmation process. The centre's current booking instructions decide which documents or records it needs for registration.
+The exam owner explains the product and general format. The selected centre controls its own booking and test-day administration. The German mission controls the visa-file document instructions and decides recognition of language proof for the application. One document may be useful at one stage but irrelevant at another. For example, a booking email is evidence of registration, not automatically a visa document; a course record is not automatically an exam certificate.
 
-Match the correct exam to your plan, then save the confirmation email and the centre's cancellation or rescheduling policy. Ask the centre before paying if the name in your booking will not match your passport.
+### Register with consistent identity details
 
-## Before test day
+Use the legal spelling shown on the identification you will present, save the confirmation, and query the centre before paying if a mismatch exists. Do not infer an ID rule from another centre. Ask the selected centre what exact identification document it currently requires and keep its answer with the booking records.
 
-Check the centre's message again. You may need the original accepted ID or passport, your booking confirmation, and any centre-specific instruction. Confirm arrival time, location, and what items are allowed or prohibited.
+### Build the visa-file list only from the mission
 
-Do not assume a photocopy will replace the original ID, or that a rule at another centre applies to yours. The local centre controls its own check-in instructions.
+When you receive a certificate, compare its details with your own identity record and read the responsible mission’s current checklist. The mission, not the provider or centre, tells you what it currently asks for in the visa file, including any document form or additional evidence. If the page is unclear, ask through the mission’s official contact route.
 
-## Before the visa appointment
+## Three-stage document map
 
-Keep the original certificate and a clear copy together. Check the certificate name against the applicant's identity details, and note its examination date and issuing institution.
+| Stage | Ask the owner | Save privately |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Booking | Selected centre: registration and identity instruction | Booking page, reply, confirmation |
+| Test day | Selected centre: arrival, identification, permitted items | Current centre instruction |
+| Visa file | Competent mission: certificate acceptance and document form | Mission checklist/reply |
 
-Before submitting anything, check whether the responsible German mission accepts that certificate for your specific family reunion case and whether its current checklist asks for originals, copies, translations, or additional documents. Requirements can differ by location and individual circumstances.
+Never promote an item from one column to another without the owner’s current instruction.
 
-## Keep a private document record
+## Pre-payment stop gate
 
-Keep the official booking email, centre instructions, certificate details, and official mission checklist together in a private folder. Record where each requirement came from and when you checked it.
+Do not pay until each of these has an observable record: the exact adult exam product, a path from the exam owner to the selected centre, the selected centre's current booking name and identification instruction, the fee and currency, the payment recipient or channel, the cancellation or rescheduling terms, and the way a registration result is communicated. An unanswered item that could affect admission, loss of money, or the route timeline is a stop condition.
 
-Do not send passport images, certificate scans, or booking codes to an unverified agent or group chat just to ask a general question. Ask the official centre or mission through its published contact route when a document rule is unclear.
+The selected centre's current identity and booking instruction applies only to that centre and session; it is not a universal passport, ID, copy, photograph, or materials rule. If another centre says something different, keep both instructions attached to their owners instead of choosing the more convenient version.
 
-## Common mistakes
+| Atomic check | Complete only when |
+| --- | --- |
+| Product and centre | The exact adult product and dated official path to the selected centre are saved. |
+| Name and identification | The booking spelling matches the identification the selected centre says it will check, or the centre has resolved the mismatch in writing. |
+| Transaction | The current fee, currency, payment route, cancellation and rescheduling terms are saved from the selected centre. |
+| Test day | The selected centre's current arrival, identification and permitted-items instructions are saved for later reopening. |
+| Submission | The competent mission's route-specific checklist is saved separately; this page is not a complete visa-document list. |
 
-- A booking name that does not match the passport.
-- Taking only a copy when the centre expects original identification.
-- Missing a centre email about check-in or permitted items.
-- Treating a course completion document as an official exam certificate.
-- Assuming every German mission accepts the same proof in the same way.
+### Scenario: the booking name differs before payment
+
+Stop before payment if possible and ask the selected centre, through its published channel, how it handles the discrepancy. Record the exact spelling used in the booking, the identification you plan to present, and the reply. Do not guess that a minor difference is acceptable or that a photocopy solves it. Separately, keep the mission’s visa-file requirements out of this centre conversation.
+
+### Scenario: payment was already sent before a mismatch was found
+
+Do not submit a second booking, reverse a payment, alter an identity record, or assume that entry or a refund is guaranteed. Save the booking confirmation and payment evidence privately, then use the selected centre's published channel to report the exact mismatch and ask for its correction, cancellation, transfer or other current process. Mark the item unresolved until that centre replies. If the correction changes the test or result timeline, recalculate the plan; it still does not change what the mission accepts for the visa file.
+
+### Scenario: a centre email asks for identification but the mission checklist says nothing about it
+
+Follow the centre email for test-day administration and retain it. The absence of an ID instruction on a mission page does not cancel a centre’s test-day requirement. Conversely, a centre instruction is not a visa submission checklist. Treat the two lists as parallel, owned workflows.
+
+### Scenario: you have received a certificate
+
+Save the certificate securely, note the issuing institution and date, and compare the printed name with your identity record. Then check the responsible mission’s current page or ask it whether the certificate form and any copies, translations or other evidence are requested for your route. Do not assert that an original, a digital copy, a translation, or a certificate duration will be accepted without that instruction.
+
+## Name-match check
+
+Make a three-column comparison: booking name, identification name, certificate name. Copy characters exactly and add one source link or document reference for every entry. If any field differs, ask the owner of the affected stage. This is a practical consistency check, not a declaration that a mismatch will be rejected or accepted.
+
+## Source-and-copy log
+
+For each document, write: what it is, which stage it belongs to, who instructed it, URL/reply reference, checked date, and whether you hold an original or copy. Store sensitive passport images, certificate scans and booking codes privately; do not send them to unverified agents or public chats to obtain general advice.
+
+## Mistakes to avoid
+
+- Treating a course completion document as the required language certificate.
+- Assuming a booking confirmation proves the visa-file requirement.
+- Copying an ID rule from a different city or provider.
+- Ignoring a spelling difference until arrival at the centre.
+- Asking a centre to decide certificate acceptance for the visa file.
+- Sending sensitive records through an unofficial contact channel.
 
 ## Next action
 
-Read [German family reunion language requirement](/guides/german-family-reunion-language-requirement/) before deciding which proof you need. Then use [Goethe A1 test centers](/guides/goethe-a1-test-centers/) to confirm local rules and [Goethe A1 booking mistakes](/guides/goethe-a1-booking-mistakes/) for a final booking check.
+Complete the three-stage map using a single selected centre and the competent mission’s current route page. Then return to [Goethe A1 test centers](/guides/goethe-a1-test-centers/) for local verification or to [German A1 exam booking timeline](/guides/german-a1-exam-booking-timeline/) to connect only confirmed document and date dependencies.
 
-## Official sources
+## Four-owner responsibility map
 
-- [Goethe-Institut German examinations](https://www.goethe.de/en/spr/prf.html)
-- [BAMF family reunification](https://www.bamf.de/EN/Themen/MigrationAufenthalt/ZuwandererDrittstaaten/Familie/familie-node.html)
-- [German Federal Foreign Office: proof of German language skills FAQ](https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/visa-service/buergerservice/faq/01a-deutschkenntnisse-606682) — use the responsible mission's current checklist for the visa file.
+This document map keeps four owners separate. **National/orientation authority:** BAMF and the Foreign Office describe the language-proof framework and direct a reader to the competent route. **Competent mission or receiving authority:** specifies the visa-file instruction for the reader’s route, including any certificate question. **Exam owner:** identifies the examination and offers general product material without deciding a submission list. **Selected centre and reader:** the centre gives its current registration and test-day document instructions; the reader protects private records, compares names across documents, logs their source/date, and asks the owner of the affected stage when an item conflicts.
+
+## Official sources
 
-## A1 route FAQ
+- [Federal Foreign Office language-skills FAQ](https://www.auswaertiges-amt.de/en/visa-service/buergerservice/faq/01a-deutschkenntnisse-606682) — checked 2026-09-09; supports using the responsible mission for route guidance.
+- [BAMF language-proof leaflet](https://www.bamf.de/SharedDocs/Anlagen/DE/MigrationAufenthalt/Ehegattennachzug/ehegattennachzug-en.pdf?__blob=publicationFile&v=11) — last successful content check 2026-09-01; supports the mission’s recognition role, not a personal document list. The direct PDF returned HTTP 403 during the 2026-09-09 recheck, so do not treat reachability as freshly confirmed.
+- [Goethe German examinations](https://www.goethe.de/en/spr/prf.html) — checked 2026-09-09; supports the exam-owner boundary and local-centre contact route.
+- [telc examination-centre finder](https://www.telc.net/en/language-examinations/find-a-telc-examination-centre/) — checked 2026-09-09; supports contacting the chosen centre for its local procedures.
 
-### Can this page confirm the documents for my case?
+## A private review before each stage
 
-No. It separates the questions you need to ask; the official centre and the German mission or authority decide their current document instructions.
+Before registering, read only the booking row of your map and check that the centre, exact product and identity question belong together. Before travelling, read only the test-day row and reopen the selected centre’s most recent instruction. Before preparing the visa file, read only the mission row and reopen the mission’s current route-specific page. This sequence reduces the temptation to carry an instruction from one stage into another.
 
-### What if local instructions conflict?
+If you use a representative, translator, or family member for practical help, keep ownership clear. They can help you organise a file or read a page, but their summary is not the source. Save the original official link or reply where you can reopen it. Use secure private storage for sensitive items. Do not include passport numbers, booking codes, certificate serial information, or scans in a general planning sheet shared with people who do not need them.
 
-Pause, save the official links or written replies, and ask the responsible source which instruction applies before booking or submitting documents.
+When a page is unavailable, do not substitute a cached copy or an anecdote for current instruction. Record the page as unavailable, use the official published contact route, and wait for a response appropriate to the stage. The document map should make uncertainty visible early enough to avoid a preventable booking or submission error.
 
-## A1 decision tools and next steps
+Use a separate folder or labelled envelope for each stage, but do not discard earlier evidence after a later stage is complete. A booking confirmation can help explain a centre query; a current centre instruction can help you prepare for test day; a mission checklist controls the visa-file assembly. Their value is different. Date each saved item and periodically remove access for anyone who no longer needs to help you organise it. This is ordinary privacy hygiene, not a substitute for any official identity or document-security instruction.
 
-These planning aids organise questions; they do not decide an exemption, certificate acceptance, fees, result timing, or your individual case.
+When a translated explanation conflicts with the official original, preserve both but seek clarification from the source that owns the stage. Do not ask a translator to decide an immigration rule or a centre to interpret a mission checklist. A document log is most useful when it shows exactly who supplied each instruction and when it was last checked.
 
-- Return to the [Germany A1 family reunion hub](/germany-family-reunion-a1/) to see the full decision order.
-- Start with [Route Finder](/tools/route-finder/) if the requirement or exemption question is still open.
-- Turn your official checks into a working list with the [Checklist Generator](/tools/checklist-generator/).
-- Enter only locally confirmed buffers in the [Timeline Calculator](/tools/timeline-calculator/).
-- Compare the questions—not provider rankings—in [Exam Comparison](/tools/exam-comparison/).
-- The [A1 Family Reunion Pack](/contact/?interest=a1-family-reunion-pack) is a proposed planning pack; requesting access only opens a contact-intent path.
-- [Route Review](/contact/?interest=route-review) is proposed informational support, not legal, visa, or acceptance advice.
+If you receive a new instruction, add it rather than overwriting the old entry. Mark which one is current and why, so the checklist continues to show a transparent, dated decision trail.
