+## Decision log
+
+For every answer, keep four fields: the page or written reply, its date, the decision it supports, and what it does not decide. For example, a mission reply may support “certificate requested for this route” but not the next local exam date. A Goethe or telc page may support a product description but not a mission’s acceptance decision. This simple split prevents a source from being stretched beyond its authority.
+
+## Mistakes to avoid
+
+- Treating every “family reunion” label as the same legal route.
+- Reading a national FAQ as a personal exemption decision.
+- Letting a school, broker, or test centre decide what a mission accepts.
+- Booking a product before the exact proof question is resolved.
+- Saving only a screenshot without the URL and date checked.
+- Treating a delayed reply as confirmation.
+
+## Next action
+
+Save the current mission instruction for your route, complete the worksheet, and send the narrow question if anything remains unclear. If you already hold a certificate, use the separate [existing-certificate check](/guides/goethe-a1-germany-family-reunion/) before treating it as usable proof; it is a sibling check, not the next step in the seven-pillar preparation sequence. Only after the mission or competent authority has given you a usable instruction should you compare exact A1 products in [Goethe A1 vs telc A1](/guides/goethe-a1-vs-telc-a1/). If the route category itself is still unclear, use [Route Finder](/tools/route-finder/) to organise the questions you must verify. The [Checklist Generator](/tools/checklist-generator/) is also a private planning aid; neither tool decides your route.
+
+## Four-owner responsibility map
+
+This route map has four different owners. **National orientation authority:** the Federal Foreign Office and BAMF explain the general legal framework and direct readers toward the appropriate route. **Competent receiving authority:** the German mission where the application is filed, and where relevant the competent immigration authority, decide the route-specific language-proof and document instruction. **Exam owner:** Goethe or telc can identify an examination product and its published standards. **Selected centre and reader:** the centre controls its own booking and test-day process; the reader records facts, asks the mission’s narrow question, and does not convert a general explanation into an exemption or outcome.
