+
+Keep the completed board as a snapshot, not a substitute for a current local instruction. A later authority reply can change one card without deciding every other card. The four-owner map tells you whether to ask the authority, an exam owner or a centre; it does not let the checklist infer an approval from a blank or conflicting entry.
+
+## Next action
+
+This is the terminal review step. Where the gap concerns the route, return to the [settlement route guide](/guides/goethe-b1-germany-settlement-work/) or [citizenship language-proof guide](/guides/germany-b1-citizenship-language-proof/). Where the gap is only an exam-centre date or term, verify directly with the selected centre rather than reopening the legal-route sequence.
+
+## Source boundaries and recheck
+
+The listed statutes support their own general provisions, not a conclusion that every application condition is met. A federal orientation page can help locate the process, but cannot authoritatively replace a local authority’s current form, portal or written instruction. An exam owner can confirm what it calls a product; the receiving authority must confirm whether that item is sufficient in the exact format supplied. Put this boundary in the status field, not only in a footnote.
+
+Recheck before submitting whenever a document has changed, an instruction is older than your record, the authority and provider wording conflict, or a date matters to your plan. Use the owner named on the disputed claim. Preserve the authority reply and product or centre source as dated evidence. This checklist deliberately never converts a missing answer into a recommendation to submit, pay, or infer approval.
