-## The useful answer is not one number
+## Who this is for
 
-Do not use an old blog price as your Germany A1 budget. The usable fee is the one the official local test centre publishes for the exact exam, date, and booking route you plan to use.
+Use this page only after you have identified **Goethe-Zertifikat A1: Start Deutsch 1** as an exact product to investigate and have a real location in mind. It gives four source-checked 2026 price records from two official Goethe scopes: the Goethe-Institut Germany price page and the named Goethe-Institut Beijing registration page. It is not a worldwide fee table.
 
-For an adult Goethe route, check that the listing says **Goethe-Zertifikat A1: Start Deutsch 1**. The Goethe examinations overview can help you identify the adult A1 examination and reach a Goethe-Institut or exam partner; it cannot give your local fee or booking terms.
+The records help you understand which category question to ask and what evidence to save. They do not decide whether a German mission accepts the certificate, whether you qualify for a learner category, what a partner centre will charge, whether tax or another checkout item applies, or whether a seat exists. The selected official or authorised centre remains the final source for its transaction.
 
-## Why one global price does not work
+## Key decisions
 
-Official Goethe pages publish different local price tables for Germany and for the Beijing institute. The Beijing page also distinguishes locally defined learner categories. These first-party examples show why a price from one location or category must not be copied into another booking.
