+“Germany” below means the 2026 scope of the Goethe-Institut Germany price page. “Beijing” means the named Goethe-Institut Beijing page. Beijing is not a substitute for a China-wide price, and the Germany page does not establish the checkout of every independent exam partner. If your intended centre is outside those exact scopes, use the fallback rather than copying the nearest number.
 
-## Before you pay
+### Treat category status as a question
 
-Confirm the exam name and level, official local centre, test date, payment deadline, and result process. Then read the centre's cancellation or refund rule and its rescheduling rule before completing payment.
+The Germany page defines its own course-participant window. The Beijing page publishes a separate current-learner explanation and evidence instructions. Those source-controlled category definitions appear in the versioned table below only while their records remain current. VisaLang does not decide whether you meet either definition. Your booking channel must apply the category to the intended exam.
 
