-## What "official test centre" means
+## Who this is for
 
-An official centre is a Goethe-Institut or exam partner shown or confirmed through the official Goethe route, or a telc examination centre reached through the official [telc centre finder](https://www.telc.net/en/language-examinations/find-a-telc-examination-centre/). A German class provider is not automatically an official exam provider.
+Use this page once the authority-provided proof question has produced an exact exam product to investigate. It is for readers who need to distinguish an official Goethe route or telc examination centre from a course provider, copied directory, agent advertisement, or expired listing. It cannot certify a centre for you; authorisation, offerings and local administrative terms are confirmed through the provider and the selected centre.
 
-Goethe says its German examinations are offered through Goethe-Instituts and exam partners. Use the official provider's route, then check the selected local centre's own exam listing. Do not rely on a copied address, an old directory, or a course advert.
+## Key decisions
 
-As a bounded China example, the official [Goethe-Institut Beijing examination and registration page](https://www.goethe.de/ins/cn/zh/spr/prf/anm.html) publishes its own current exam products, dates, prices, forms, and contact route. Those details support checks for the Beijing institute only and must not be carried over to another city or centre.
+### Verify the provider route first
 
-## Verify the exact examination
+Goethe says its German examinations can be taken at Goethe-Instituts and exam partners. Start on the official Goethe examinations route, then follow it to the selected local centre. For telc, use telc’s official finder. A page that sells German lessons may be useful for study, but it is not evidence that it administers the correct certificate exam.
 
-For the adult Goethe route, look for **Goethe-Zertifikat A1: Start Deutsch 1**. Do not assume that every A1 listing, youth version, course, or mock test is the certificate you need.
+### Match the full product name
 
-For telc, use the finder to reach a centre, check the exact local A1 product, and ask the responsible authority whether that certificate is suitable for your own family reunion case. This guide does not decide telc acceptance for an embassy or visa file.
+For the adult Goethe route, check for **Goethe-Zertifikat A1: Start Deutsch 1**, rather than a children’s/young-people’s exam, an A1 course, or sample training. For telc, identify the exact product the centre lists and return to the responsible mission if the product is not already confirmed. A centre’s presence in a finder does not make every product on its page acceptable for every visa file.
 
-## Use the checks in order
+### Keep local terms local
 
-1. Confirm the authority's accepted proof for your case.
-2. Match it to the exact adult product; for Goethe this is **Goethe-Zertifikat A1: Start Deutsch 1**.
-3. Reach an official Goethe-Institut/exam partner or telc centre through the provider's official route.
-4. Get the local terms directly from that selected centre.
+The selected centre owns its current calendar, seats, payment path, identity instruction, test-day directions, cancellation conditions, results process and certificate collection or delivery process. Ask the centre and save its answer. Do not copy a fee, deadline, ID rule or result claim from another city, another provider, or a general page.
 
-## Centre-selection checklist
+## Germany fee route
 
-Before booking, get the following directly from the selected local centre:
+Open the [Goethe-Institut Germany 2026 fee page](https://www.goethe.de/ins/de/en/prf/pre.html), locate the adult Goethe-Zertifikat A1 (Start Deutsch 1 / SD1) row, and read the course-participant remark. Then continue to the selected official Goethe-Institut Germany booking route and confirm the category, any tax or checkout detail, the intended session and the final amount. The country price page does not prove every exam partner uses that checkout.
 
-- Whether the centre offers the correct A1 exam and is confirmed through the official provider.
-- The current exam date and registration deadline.
-- Whether speaking is held on the same day or arranged separately.
-- The stated result timing and certificate collection or delivery process.
-- ID requirements, the spelling of your name, payment rules, and the centre's test-day instructions.
+## Beijing fee route
 
-The local centre controls its current date, fee, registration, ID, result, and certificate process, as well as its other booking terms. Check these from the local centre, not from a general international overview.
+Open the [Goethe-Institut Beijing schedule and registration page](https://www.goethe.de/ins/cn/zh/spr/prf/anm.html), match the adult A1/SD1 row, read the local learner-category definition, and follow the current form and registration-result process. Beijing evidence is not a China-wide price or category rule. A listed amount does not guarantee a seat; wait for the official registration and payment notice and recheck local terms before paying.
 
-## When the centre page is unclear
+## Official-centre verification record
 
-Ask the centre one precise question at a time: whether it offers the adult A1 exam, the next bookable date, whether speaking is separate, the registration deadline, and how results or certificates are issued.
+| Check | Evidence to save | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Provider route reached from Goethe/telc official page | URL and checked date |  |
+| Exact adult exam shown | Centre page or written reply |  |
+| Centre contact route | Official page |  |
+| Correct product accepted by authority | Mission/authority source |  |
+| Current local terms requested | Dated centre reply |  |
 
-Keep the reply with your booking record. A vague answer about a German course, an A1 class, or an enquiry list is not the same as confirmation of an examination place.
+This record separates “I found a location” from “I have verified an examinable, relevant product.”
 
-## Common booking mistakes
+### Scenario: a nearby school offers an A1 package
 
-- Enrolling in a German course when you need an examination booking.
-- Choosing the wrong level, exam provider, or A1 version.
-- Assuming a nearby location is an official examination centre.
-- Ignoring result timing until after a visa appointment is booked.
-- Leaving the name mismatch between the booking and passport unresolved.
+The school advertises an A1 course with a “certificate.” Ask whether it administers the exact examination, whether its site is reached through the official provider route, and who owns the booking. If it is a course only, it may support preparation but does not solve your examination search. Keep the course decision separate from the certificate and mission-acceptance decisions.
+
+### Scenario: a directory lists a centre but the centre page has no A1 date
+
+The directory is a lead, not proof of a seat or scheduled product. Reach the centre through the official provider path, then use its published contact channel to ask whether it currently offers the exact exam and how it announces registration. Leave the date unknown until the centre confirms it.
+
+### Scenario: the centre gives a different ID instruction from another centre
+
+Follow the selected centre’s current written instruction and clarify ambiguity directly with it. Identity check-in is a local execution rule. Do not promise that any particular passport, national ID, copy, or spelling correction will be accepted; ask the centre which exact identification it currently requires for the booking.
+
+## Centre-contact script
+
+> I am considering [exact product] at your centre. Please confirm whether you currently administer that exam and provide the official page for registration, current test-day identification, result/certificate process, and any cancellation or rescheduling terms. I will confirm visa acceptance with the responsible German mission.
+
+This asks for operational facts without inviting the centre to decide an immigration outcome.
+
+## Booking evidence pack
+
+Keep the provider-finder link, centre page, dated screenshots or PDFs, contact reply, booking confirmation, and payment record together. Add the exact name entered in booking and the identity document you plan to use. This pack helps you resolve a mismatch early; it does not replace the mission’s visa checklist.
+
+## Booking failure recovery
+
+### Scenario: a name mismatch is found before payment
+
+Pause the transaction. Compare the booking spelling with the identification that this selected centre says it will check, then ask through the centre's published channel how to correct the record. A rule from another centre is not evidence for this booking. Continue only when the current centre has supplied an observable correction or instruction that you can save.
+
+### Scenario: payment already sent before the mismatch is found
+
+Keep the confirmation and payment evidence private and contact the selected centre through the same verified official route. Ask what correction, cancellation, transfer or other process applies to this booking; do not create a duplicate booking, dispute the transaction, travel to the exam, or claim a refund outcome on the basis of this guide. Mark the issue unresolved until the centre answers, and recalculate any affected test, result or certificate plan.
+
+### Scenario: the booking confirmation names a different product or session
+
+Do not treat payment as proof that the correct exam has been booked. Send the centre the exact product and session shown in its confirmation, ask it to identify the current resolution route, and preserve both the original offer and the confirmation. If the product differs from what the receiving authority confirmed, return the acceptance question to that authority after the centre has clarified what was actually booked.
+
+## Mistakes to avoid
+
+- Booking a class instead of an examination.
+- Assuming a centre listed for one product offers every A1 version.
+- Calling an old directory an official provider confirmation.
+- Transferring fee, seat, date, ID or certificate rules from another centre.
+- Booking a visa appointment around an unconfirmed result process.
+- Ignoring a spelling mismatch until test day.
 
